From: ViKing <viking.yfy@qq.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 23:42:17 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] rtl837x: preserve C-tags on CPU egress to user ports

The CPU sends packets with a service tag that selects the user port.
When the port is in a VLAN-aware bridge without VID 1, the switch
adds the CPU PVID (1) to otherwise untagged packets sent by Linux.

Enable C-tag retention from the CPU port to user ports so a frame
keeps the customer tagging chosen by the software bridge.

Signed-off-by: ViKing <viking.yfy@qq.com>

--- a/src/rtl837x_policy.c
+++ b/src/rtl837x_policy.c
@@ -892,6 +892,17 @@ int rtl837x_local_init(struct dsa_switch
 	ret = rtl837x_seed_vlan_table(gsw);
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;
+
+	/* The CPU service tag selects the user port. Keep the C-tag
+	 * chosen by Linux, including the absence of a tag.
+	 */
+	dsa_switch_for_each_user_port(dp, ds) {
+		ret = rtl837x_vlan_port_set_egress_vlan_keep(priv, gsw->cpu_port,
+							     dp->index, true);
+		if (ret)
+			return ret;
+	}
+
 	dsa_switch_for_each_available_port(dp, ds) {
 		ret = rtl837x_set_stp_state(gsw, dp->index,
 			dsa_port_is_cpu(dp) ? BR_STATE_FORWARDING : BR_STATE_DISABLED);
